# Weaver And Tunnel Model

Weaver provides remote execution environments; WireGuard surfaces provide secure transport paths.

## Weaver model

- Weaver creation is requested via CLI/API and provisioned by server-side infrastructure.
- Sessions are listed, attached, and deleted through `loom weaver *` and `/api/weaver*` routes.
- Web surfaces mirror this state at `/weavers` and `/weavers/:weaverId`.

## Attach paths

- `loom weaver attach <id>` (or `loom attach <id>`) for interactive attach.
- `loom ssh <id>` for SSH entry over managed connectivity.

## WireGuard tunnel model

- Device registry establishes trusted client identities.
- Session creation links device-to-weaver tunnel endpoints.
- DERP map route supports relay path discovery.

Key API family:

- `/api/wg/devices*`
- `/api/wg/sessions*`
- `/api/wg/derp-map`

## Operational constraints

- Tunnel-up currently targets one weaver at a time.
- Stale devices/sessions should be revoked/deleted to reduce drift.

<Callout variant="tip" title="Operational split">
	Think of Weaver as compute lifecycle and WireGuard as transport lifecycle. They interact, but they are not the same control surface.
</Callout>
